l.","Cost: findings are heuristics; lint.ignore and lint.topics tune them per project."],"criteria":[]},"sections":[{"id":"A","title":"Decision"},{"id":"B","title":"Options"},{"id":"C","title":"Consequences"}],"text":"Decision span=3 A language-agnostic core compares what crux files declare with facts from the code: modules and imports, HTTP routes, gRPC services, topics and queues with their side, technologies, deployables and infrastructure. Built-in adapters cover Go, TypeScript/JavaScript and infra files; any other language plugs in a command that prints the facts JSON. Options span=3 Option Pros Cons Fit --- --- --- --- A — Pattern adapters in the binary + command plug-ins No toolchain needed; fast (2.6 s on 2,600 Go files). Patterns miss wrapped clients; config adds more. ok B — Full type-checked analysis (go/packages, tsc) Exact. Needs toolchains and builds; slow; per-language depth. warn C — No code checks Simple. Docs drift silently. no Consequences span=3 - Positive: drift shows up as lint findings with a fix line; crux scan feeds the adopt skill. - Cost: findings are heuristics; lint.ignore and lint.topics tune them per project."},"source":"---\ntitle: Code facts come from language adapters; lint compares docs with code\nstatus: Accepted\ndate: 2026-10-06\nauthor: abtin\ntags: [lint, scan]\ncomponents: [scanner, linter]\napplies_to: [internal/scan/**, internal/lint/**]\nreopen_when: [\"a team needs a language without an adapter and a facts-printing command is not enough\"]\n---\n\n## Decision {span=3}\n```callout ok Decision\nA language-agnostic core compares what crux files declare with facts from the code: modules and imports, HTTP routes, gRPC services, topics and queues with their side, technologies, deployables and infrastructure. Built-in adapters cover Go, TypeScript/JavaScript and infra files; any other language plugs in a command that prints the facts JSON.\n```\n\n## Options {span=3}\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Fit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A — Pattern adapters in the binary + command plug-ins | No toolchain needed; fast (2.6 s on 2,600 Go files). | Patterns miss wrapped clients; config adds more. | ok |\n| B — Full type-checked analysis (go/packages, tsc) | Exact. | Needs toolchains and builds; slow; per-language depth. | warn |\n| C — No code checks | Simple. | Docs drift silently. | no |\n\n## Consequences {span=3}\n- Positive: drift shows up as lint findings with a fix line; `crux scan` feeds the adopt skill.\n- Cost: findings are heuristics; `lint.ignore` and `lint.topics` tune them per project.\n"}